.TH AENIGMA-STANDARD-SETUP 8 "2026-08-17" "aenigma 5.0.0" "Aenigma Administration Scripts"
.SH NAME
aenigma-standard-setup \- one-time initialization of the standard aenigma onion services
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aenigma-standard-setup
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aenigma-standard-setup
performs one-time initialization of the onion services used by a standard
aenigma deployment: a public-facing onion service for the main
.I aenigma
backend, and a stealth-authenticated onion service for the
.I aenigma-dashboard
backend. Each is provisioned by invoking
.BR aenigma-tor (8)
with fixed, opinionated defaults for local address, onion port, and
(for the dashboard) client authorization.
.PP
This script assumes the underlying packages and their base configuration
have already been installed and completed independently; it does not
install or configure Tor, DNS, VPN, or any other subsystem itself beyond
invoking
.BR aenigma-tor (8)
for these two specific services. It is intentionally narrow in scope, not
a full-system provisioning entry point, though it may grow to cover
additional one-time initialization steps in the future.
.PP
.B aenigma-standard-setup
must be run as root, since
.BR aenigma-tor (8)
itself requires root.
.SH OPTIONS
This script takes no options or arguments.
.TP
.B \-h
Not applicable; the script has no option parsing and no help output of
its own.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, or nothing needed to be done because both services were already
fully provisioned.
.TP
.B 1
Not invoked as root, or one of the underlying
.BR aenigma-tor (8)
invocations failed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.IB /var/lib/tor/aenigma/hostname
Presence of this file is treated as confirmation that the main
.I aenigma
onion service has already been fully provisioned; if missing,
.BR aenigma-tor (8)
is invoked for it again.
.TP
.IB /var/lib/tor/aenigma-dashboard/hostname
Same check, for the
.I aenigma-dashboard
onion service.
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Each service is gated on the existence of its published
.I hostname
file, not merely its service directory. This is deliberate:
.BR aenigma-tor (8)
creates and takes ownership of a service's directory early in its own
run, before Tor has been restarted and the address has actually been
generated, so a directory left behind by a previously failed or
interrupted run would otherwise be mistaken for a completed one and
never retried on a subsequent run of this script.
.IP \(bu 2
The dashboard service is provisioned with client authorization for a
user named
.IR aenigma-dashboard ,
via
.BR aenigma-tor (8) 's
.B \-u
option. Per
.BR aenigma-tor-auth (8) ,
if this script is re-run after the dashboard's
.I hostname
file already exists, the dashboard branch is skipped entirely and the
existing client authorization key is left untouched.
.IP \(bu 2
Only the main
.I aenigma
service's onion address is written into the aenigma configuration
(via
.BR aenigma-tor (8) 's
.B \-c 1 );
the dashboard's address is not, consistent with it being reached only by
authorized clients rather than referenced by the application itself.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aenigma-tor (8),
.BR aenigma-tor-auth (8),
.BR aenigma-config (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Romulus-Emanuel Ruja <romulus.rujas@aenigma.ro>